## Example Session Summary

```markdown
# Session 2 Summary: Phase 1 (POST /posts)

## Overview
Implemented blog post creation endpoint with full JPA integration, authentication, and controller test coverage.

## Implementation Details

### Database Changes
- Created posts table via migration: V2__create_posts_table.sql
- Added indexes on author_id and created_at
- Flyway applied successfully on application startup

### Entities Created
- Post (src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/model/Post.java): JPA entity
- CreatePostRequest (src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/web/dto/CreatePostRequest.java): request DTO
- PostResponse (src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/web/dto/PostResponse.java): response DTO

### Repository Methods
- PostRepository extends JpaRepository<Post, UUID> — save()/findById() provided free
- PostRepository.findByAuthorIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc() — derived query method
- File: src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/repository/PostRepository.java

### Service Layer
- PostService.createPost() - business logic for post creation, @Transactional
- Includes error handling and SLF4J logging
- File: src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/service/PostService.java

### API Endpoint
- POST /api/posts
- Request: CreatePostRequest (title, content, authorId)
- Response: PostResponse (postId, title, content, authorId, createdAt)
- Authentication: Required (JWT Bearer token via Spring Security)
- File: src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/web/PostController.java

## Tests

### Controller Tests
- PostControllerTest::createPost_returnsCreatedPost - success case
- PostControllerTest::createPost_validation_blankTitleReturns400 - validation
- PostControllerTest::createPost_unauthorized_returns401 - auth requirement
- All tests passing: YES

### Unit Tests
- PostServiceTest - service layer with mocked repository
- Coverage: 95% of service methods

## Shared Libraries

### Available for Next Sessions
- PostRepository - can be used for GET /posts/{id} in Session 3
- PostService - can be extended with getPost() method
- Post entity - represents the core post concept

### Dependencies
- No new packages added
- No new environment variables needed

## Known Limitations

### Current Implementation
- Only creation implemented, no read/update/delete yet
- No support for tags or categories
- No content length validation beyond jakarta.validation
- No duplicate post prevention

### Technical Debt
- Consider adding content sanitization
- May need to add a post status field (draft/published)
- Service layer could benefit from a dedicated mapper class

## Next Phase Recommendations

### Suggested Next Session
Session 3: Phase 2 (GET /posts/{id})
- Depends on Session 2 (need posts to read)
- Simple implementation (reuse PostRepository)
- High user value (view created posts)
- Session plan: plan/sessions/session-3-phase-2.md

### Prerequisite Work
- Add PostService.getPost() method
- Add GET endpoint to PostController
- Write controller test for retrieval

## Learnings and Gotchas

### What Worked Well
- DTO/Entity separation prevented `@Entity` leaking into the API contract
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` made service testing trivial with plain `new`
- TDD approach caught a missing `@Valid` annotation early
- `@Transactional` on the service made rollback behavior predictable

### Challenges Encountered
- Initial confusion about where `@Transactional` should live (service, not controller)
- Needed `GenerationType.UUID` (not `IDENTITY`) to generate UUID primary keys
- Testcontainers required Docker to be running locally

### Time Estimates
- Estimated time: 25 minutes
- Actual time: 30 minutes
- Variance: +5 minutes for debugging UUID generation strategy

## Code Quality Metrics

### Formatting
- Spotless applied: YES
- Checkstyle passing: YES
- Javadoc coverage: 100% of public methods

### Testing
- Controller test coverage: 3 scenarios
- Unit test coverage: 95%
- All tests passing: YES

## Files Changed

### Created
- src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/model/Post.java
- src/main/java/com/example/blogapi/repository/PostRepository.java
